1	//! [`EgressProxy`] — an explicit forward proxy that enforces an [`EgressPolicy`]
2	//! on outbound traffic from the microVM tier. HTTPS is tunneled via `CONNECT`;
3	//! the destination host is checked against the domain allow/deny policy and
4	//! the resolved IPs are checked against the SSRF (private-range) block before
5	//! any upstream connection is made. Plain-HTTP absolute-URI requests are also
6	//! host-checked: non-allowlisted hosts receive `403 Forbidden`; allowlisted
7	//! hosts receive `501 Not Implemented` (plain-HTTP forwarding is not supported —
8	//! `CONNECT`/HTTPS is the enforced path). Non-proxy-aware traffic is dropped by
9	//! the per-VM netns default-deny (L3/L4) before it reaches the proxy.
10	
11	use std::io;
12	use std::net::SocketAddr;
13	use std::sync::Arc;
